From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 03:16:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 128/184] segacd: CDR_LEADIN is not a lead-in

cd_lead is 2 or 20 -- the L arm of the diagnostic, how many frames
early to command the read. The macro wrapping it was called CDR_LEADIN,
and on a CD "lead-in" means the 150 frames before sector zero, which
lba_to_msf() already adds. Reading `lba - CDR_LEADIN` as a unit
conversion rather than a tuning knob nearly produced the wrong fix for
the hardware result this week. CDR_EARLY.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 75fe947..93075c4 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -1693,7 +1693,12 @@ static void cdd_ask_idle(void)
  * frames late and the sector is behind the head, and reading forward
  * never comes back to it. Twenty frames is a quarter of a second of
  * run-up and costs nothing but that. */
-#define CDR_LEADIN cd_lead
+/* How many frames early to command the read -- 2 or 20, the L arm of
+ * the diagnostic. Named CDR_EARLY until it nearly caused the wrong
+ * fix: "lead-in" on a CD means the 150 frames before sector zero, and
+ * lba_to_msf() already adds those. This is a tuning knob and reads
+ * like a unit conversion. */
+#define CDR_EARLY cd_lead
 
 /* ...and if it lands late anyway, ask again. This is the BIOS's own
  * answer: $4124 re-issues the whole read when an arriving header is not
@@ -1712,8 +1717,8 @@ static void cdr_reissue(void)
 {
     UBYTE start[3];
 
-    lba_to_msf(cdr_lbas[cdr_slot] >= CDR_LEADIN
-                   ? cdr_lbas[cdr_slot] - CDR_LEADIN : 0, start);
+    lba_to_msf(cdr_lbas[cdr_slot] >= CDR_EARLY
+                   ? cdr_lbas[cdr_slot] - CDR_EARLY : 0, start);
     cdc_hit = 0;
     cdc_ints = 0;
     cdr_seen = 0;
@@ -2204,7 +2209,7 @@ static BOOL cd_fetch(ULONG lba)
              * gap. There was a command Sega has and does not use, and
              * sending it was one of three ways this driver was moving
              * the drive around behind its own back. */
-            lba_to_msf(lba >= CDR_LEADIN ? lba - CDR_LEADIN : 0, start);
+            lba_to_msf(lba >= CDR_EARLY ? lba - CDR_EARLY : 0, start);
             cdd_ask_read(start);
             if (cd_late && !cdc_altctrl)
                 cd_ctrl2_wait = 1;
